  "claim": "Johannes Megapolensis served for three-and-a-half-years at the first permanent Dutch settlement in New Netherland.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Johannes Megapolensis. Sentence: Johannes Megapolensis (1603–1670) was a \"dominie\" (pastor) of the Dutch Reformed Church in the Dutch colony of New Netherland (present-day New York state in the United States), beginning in 1642.\nPage: Johannes Megapolensis. Sentence: Serving for several years at Fort Orange (present-day Albany, New York) on the upper Hudson River, he is credited with being the first Protestant missionary to the Indians in North America.\nPage: Fort Orange (New Netherland). Sentence: Fort Orange (Dutch: \"Fort Oranje\" ) was the first permanent Dutch settlement in New Netherland; the present-day city of Albany, New York developed at this site.",
